# RFC, issue, and version backlog doc management

Indexes: [RFC](../../docs/rfc/README.md) · [issues](../../docs/issues/README.md) · [backlog](../../docs/backlog/README.md)

## Golden rule

**Every doc has a status tag in the filename. Tag must match `**Status:**` in the body.**

Update the folder README index and grep cross-links in the same turn as any rename.

---

## Backlog (`docs/backlog/`)

**One file per release version** (e.g. `0.7.6-[open].md`). The file body is that version's ship checklist.

### Filename tags

`[draft]` · `[open]` · `[partial]` · `[done]` (in `done/`) · `[canceled]` (in `canceled/`)

Pattern: `{semver}-[{status}].md` — e.g. `0.7.6-[draft].md`

### Body `**Status:**` ↔ filename

| Body status | Filename | Location |
|-------------|----------|----------|
| `draft` | `X.Y.Z-[draft].md` | Version scoped, not started |
| `open` | `X.Y.Z-[open].md` | Actively shipping |
| `partial` | `X.Y.Z-[partial].md` | Release in progress |
| `done` | `X.Y.Z-[done].md` | `docs/backlog/done/` |
| `canceled` | `X.Y.Z-[canceled].md` | `docs/backlog/canceled/` — version dropped, will not ship |

### Lifecycle

```
plan version   →  0.7.6-[draft].md
start release  →  0.7.6-[open].md
in progress    →  0.7.6-[partial].md
shipped        →  done/0.7.6-[done].md
dropped        →  canceled/0.7.6-[canceled].md
```

---

## RFCs (`docs/rfc/`)

Feature **specs** — numbered RFCs, not semver files.

### Filename tags

`[draft]` · `[planned]` · `[open]` · `[partial]` · `[fixed]` (in `fixed/`) · `[canceled]` (in `canceled/`)

| Body status | Filename tag | Location |
|-------------|--------------|----------|
| `draft` | `[draft]` | Spec exists; not scheduled |
| `planned` | `[planned]` | You explicitly scheduled it |
| `open` | `[open]` | Actively in progress |
| `partial` / `stub` | `[partial]` | Code started, not shippable |
| `fixed` | `[fixed]` | `docs/rfc/fixed/` |
| `canceled` | `[canceled]` | `docs/rfc/canceled/` — will not build |

---

## Issues (`docs/issues/`)

### Filename tags

`[draft]` · `[open]` · `[workaround]` · `[fixed]` (in `fixed/`) · `[canceled]` (in `canceled/`)

| Body status | Filename tag | Location |
|-------------|--------------|----------|
| `draft` | `[draft]` | Filed, not being worked |
| `open` | `[open]` | Actively fixing |
| `workaround` | `[workaround]` | Symptom fix only |
| `fixed` | `[fixed]` | `docs/issues/fixed/` |
| `canceled` | `[canceled]` | `docs/issues/canceled/` — won't fix (document why) |

Workaround requires user permission per [honesty-and-completion.mdc](./honesty-and-completion.mdc).

---

## On status change

1. Rename file (tag + move to terminal folder when `done` / `fixed` / `canceled`)
2. Update `**Status:**` in body
3. Update the folder README index
4. Grep old path in `docs/` and fix links

| Folder | Terminal folders | Terminal statuses |
|--------|------------------|-------------------|
| `backlog/` | `done/` · `canceled/` | `done` · `canceled` |
| `rfc/` | `fixed/` · `canceled/` | `fixed` · `canceled` |
| `issues/` | `fixed/` · `canceled/` | `fixed` · `canceled` |
| `migration/` | `fixed/` · `canceled/` | `fixed` · `canceled` |

## Migration (`docs/migration/`)

Engine migration phases — numbered `01`–`03`, not RFCs.

### Filename tags

`[draft]` · `[open]` · `[partial]` · `[fixed]` (in `fixed/`) · `[canceled]` (in `canceled/`)

Pattern: `NN-[{status}]-slug.md` — e.g. `01-[fixed]-rust-engine.md`

| Body status | Filename | Location |
|-------------|----------|----------|
| `draft` | `NN-[draft]-….md` | Phase scoped, not started |
| `open` | `NN-[open]-….md` | Actively migrating |
| `partial` | `NN-[partial]-….md` | In progress |
| `fixed` | `NN-[fixed]-….md` | `docs/migration/fixed/` |
| `canceled` | `NN-[canceled]-….md` | `docs/migration/canceled/` |

All current phases (1–3) are **`fixed`** in `fixed/`. Index: [migration/README.md](../../docs/migration/README.md).
